1
00:00:07,083 --> 00:00:09,683
(Leonard:)You know the best part
of working in the clean room?

2
00:00:09,686 --> 00:00:10,756
(Leonard:)No allergies.

3
00:00:10,753 --> 00:00:12,223
(Leonard:)Check it out.

4
00:00:12,222 --> 00:00:14,222
(inhales deeply)

5
00:00:14,224 --> 00:00:16,554
Oh, that-that...
that's a lot of oxygen.

6
00:00:18,294 --> 00:00:19,414
(chuckles)

7
00:00:19,411 --> 00:00:20,531
(Howard:)We should get
going to Amy's.

8
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:22,360
(Leonard:)Can you believe
there was a time

9
00:00:22,365 --> 00:00:24,365
(Leonard:)when we would have
needed an array

10
00:00:24,367 --> 00:00:26,937
(Leonard:)of giant Cherenkov telescopes
to detect cosmic particles?

11
00:00:26,936 --> 00:00:30,106
(Leonard:)And here we are building
our own multi-wire detector

12
00:00:30,106 --> 00:00:33,006
(Leonard:)like a couple of badasses.

13
00:00:33,009 --> 00:00:35,009
(Howard:)I know. If we were still single,

14
00:00:35,011 --> 00:00:38,481
(Howard:)we'd be tripping
over all that booty.

15
00:00:47,257 --> 00:00:48,777
(Leonard:)Ladies do love a man dressed
like a kitchen garbage bag.

16
00:00:48,774 --> 00:00:50,294
(Leonard:)Oh, no.

17
00:00:50,293 --> 00:00:53,263
(Howard:)How the hell
did a pigeon get in here?

18
00:00:53,263 --> 00:00:55,263
(Leonard:)You shut the loading
doors, right?
I thought you did.

19
00:00:55,265 --> 00:00:57,265
(Leonard:)Do you know what a
disaster this is?!

20
00:00:57,267 --> 00:00:59,637
(Howard:)You mean 'cause this room isn't
supposed to have dust in it,

21
00:00:59,636 --> 00:01:02,666
(Howard:)and we just let in
a flying crap machine?!

